  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The given reaction is for preparation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>DDT</mi></math> (dichlorodiphenyl trichloroethane). Complete reaction is given as follows.</p><p>(i)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0007_67065f4d257f.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 130px;\" /></p><p>(ii)&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0007_875a05bbd4c0.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 97px;\" /></p><p>Dichloro-diphenyl-trichloroethane (DDT) is prepared by heating chloral and chlorobenzene in 1:2 ratio in the presence of conc. sulphuric acid.</p><p>DDT is used as an insecticide. It is also used as a mosquito repellant.</p>"
